	• If the Turing machine eventually halts after \(N\) steps (where \(N\) could be \(10^{100}\) steps), a sudden phase transition ripples across the entire lattice, opening a finite spectral gap (\(\Delta > 0\)).

2. The Physical Consequence

Because Alan Turing proved that no algorithm can ever predict in advance whether an arbitrary program will halt, no mathematical algorithm—even if you know the exact microscopic equations of every atom to infinite precision—can ever predict the macroscopic phase of an arbitrary quantum material. A material can look completely gapless up to the size of a planet, and then suddenly snap into a gapped phase when you add one more atom!

