• When you and another observer look at the coffee cup, neither of you touches the cup directly—you each intercept a tiny, independent fraction of the scattered photons.
• Because hundreds of independent environmental fragments all carry the exact same redundant record of the pointer state, every observer extracts the identical result without disturbing the cup or each other. Objectivity is born out of consensus across environmental fragments.

