Physicists quantify Quantum Darwinism using quantum mutual information \(I(S : F)\)—measuring how much you know about a system \(S\) by capturing only a small fraction \(f\) of the total environment \(F\):
• Purely Quantum World (No Redundancy): You must capture more than 50% of the entire environment before you learn almost anything about the system; information is locked inside global quantum entanglement.
